    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "aec872a74de8bdb91275900804c4ae06779474aa419ef8ed3d3c13040c12ee81",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast, then an 8–9-hour group excursion with an English-speaking guide to the coast. Valparaíso, “Valpo” to its people, is a bohemian port city of colourful hills: not wealthy, a little dishevelled, but full of charm and proud of its past and present, often compared to a blend of Sorrento, old Lisbon and San Francisco. Its prosperous neighbour, Viña del Mar, makes a more orderly impression: the two cities complement each other perfectly.\n\nLunch (at an extra charge) at one of the coast’s renowned fish restaurants. Return to Santiago.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1NU3aFb_Gq2KBAoWRZcdXVASs6zbVSeR6",
